## Law of total probability [Thm 2.4, Eq 2.2]{.tag}

Rates are often easy within groups: per supplier, per segment.

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="58%"}
::: {.box-thm}
Let $H_1,\dots,H_n$ be a partition of $\Omega$ [(Def 1.3: no two overlap, together they make up $\Omega$)]{.muted}, all $\Prob(H_i)>0$. Then
$$\Prob(A)=\sum_{i=1}^n\Prob(A\mid H_i)\,\Prob(H_i).$$
:::
:::
::: {.column width="42%"}

::: {#a0994de7 .cell fig-height='3' fig-width='4.4' execution_count=31}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}
